# CUTLASS pin.  Header-only dependency: the build wants only
#   -I$(CUTLASS_DIR)/include -I$(CUTLASS_DIR)/tools/util/include
#
# This was a git SUBMODULE until 2026-08-23 and it cost more than it bought.
# Nothing used it AS a submodule -- `git worktree add` never populates one, and
# sparky shares a single clone via a SYMLINK at the submodule path, which git
# refuses to tolerate: every `git checkout` either failed with
#   error: expected submodule path 'cutlass' not to be a symbolic link
# or silently replaced the symlink with an empty directory.  On 2026-08-23 that
# made three consecutive gate runs test a STALE TREE while reporting 18/18, and
# put an ungated broken commit on dev.  Git no longer manages this path, so a
# checkout cannot fight the filesystem over it.
#
# This follows the precedent already set by src/cuda/mmq/VENDOR.md, which made
# the same call for the llama.cpp MMQ kernels: an external build dependency
# should not be something git has to manage.
#
# The Makefile checks the headers exist before compiling the CUTLASS TU and
# WARNS if the clone's HEAD != this sha (that check found the dev box and
# sparky on different revisions the day it was written).
#
# This sha is v4.7.0, the LATEST release as of 2026-08-23.  (sparky was already
# on it; the dev box was a release behind on v4.6.1 and AGENTS.md claimed
# v4.5.2 -- three machines, three answers, which is why the pin now exists.)
#
# POLICY: track the latest CUTLASS *release tag*, not main.  main carries
# untagged daily churn through the MXFP4 expert GEMM we depend on, and a
# moving dependency there is not something the gate suite can protect us
# from.  Bumping this sha is a real change: it is NOT byte-exact, so it
# needs a full gate run AND a decode A/B (see L096) before it lands.
#
# Point CUTLASS_DIR at a clone of this sha, or run `make cutlass`.
url=https://github.com/NVIDIA/cutlass.git
sha=dcf215af68a2d08d305076c152a06f201728cd53
